{
 "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
 "title": "dist/electo/state_meetings.json",
 "description": "{as_of, format: 2, not_read[{name,why,u}], note, bodies[body], legislature{source, meetings[]}}",
 "x-area": "export_bundle",
 "x-writer": "agencies.export_state_meetings (validate_body / validate_meeting)",
 "x-readers": "Electo ga/crawl_import.py (reads data/crawl_bundle/electo/ or data/crawl/), gc_build.py, councils.py (not pushed; read from the full bundle in crawl.yml import step)",
 "x-version": "format 2 (agencies.FMT; meta.fmt 2 in records)",
 "x-documented-in": "schema.md 'state_meetings.json (format 2)' = agencies.STATE_MEETINGS_SCHEMA",
 "x-observed": "not observed from Crawl (Electo/ga/crawl/state_meetings.json is Electo's re-written copy: agencies[] not bodies[], links {t,u})",
 "x-issues": [
  "I04 (two_versions): Three unrelated version numbers: store.SCHEMA_VERSION = 2 (kv 'schema'), export SCHEMA_VERSION '2.3' (manifest schema_version), agencies FMT = 2 (state_meetings 'format' and meta.fmt); codeacts parser 4; no other file carries a format number (DATA_FORMAT_PLAN rule 1)",
  "I05 (same_key_two_types): state_meetings.json: key x is a list of {l,u} files in bodies[].meetings[] but a bool (cancelled) in legislature.meetings[]; c (chamber) is not explained in schema.md; schema.md gives the top level as {as_of, format, note, not_read, ...} while the code writes as_of, format, not_read, note",
  "I20 (downstream_reshape): Electo's ga/crawl/state_meetings.json and meeting_summaries.json are re-written by Electo (agencies[] not bodies[], links {t,u}, dropped, legislature.hearings; summaries keyed by url under by{}), so they are not Crawl's format and were not used as evidence of it"
 ],
